    {
      "id": "fae8dd7e6fbb22316c35d51f04936cc9f7d95798",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2129174414,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Yes, the ordering in which it CMake puts those is incorrect and fundamentally broken. No matter how you specify the ordering of the flags, CMake will reorder them as part of its de-duplication process and it chooses a silly order that doesn't work. However, we set `/WX-` for those so it's not fatal for now.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-09-25T13:43:34.419Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-09-25T13:43:34.419Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 329805838,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 17404,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "aa8566777db3ba202323ce9c262388dae6f41088",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2129177105,
          "type": null,
          "body": "You can see, for example, that CMake reorders the `/wd4200` (specified at the same time as the options to change the warning level) to be earlier and in the same location. There's some nonsense you can do to turn off some of the de-duplication to work around CMake's broken behavior.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-09-25T13:44:58.728Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-09-25T13:44:58.728Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 329805838,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 17404,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "aafff98f68c4a830ce1a969b9424f844534df941",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2129184278,
          "type": null,
          "body": "MSVC is also broken; if you've explicitly disabled a warning, why should reassigning the *level* of the warning cause it to be enabled? Yes, the combination of `/W3` and `/w34100` enables C4100, but the combination in that order should not enable it.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-09-25T13:48:29.219Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-09-25T13:48:29.219Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 329805838,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 17404,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "f3d0de5f3100d76eebf7c05b3904bd94e47c6f54",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2129186598,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Of course, if we eventually get to the point of enabling `/W4` on MSVC, then we wouldn't need to change the level of those warnings, and the problem goes away.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-09-25T13:49:36.741Z",
